    "citations": [
      "Fortera has signed a multi-year agreement with Meta covering environmental attribute certificates (EACs) associated with approximately 200,000 tons of its low-carbon cement, in a deal designed to help finance production expansion.",
      "Meta will also have the option to use the cement in its own construction projects and expand the agreement’s volume or duration in future years.",
      "The partnership is expected to support development of Fortera’s planned cement plant in Ste. Genevieve, Missouri.",
      "The facility is designed to produce ReAct Cement, which uses captured carbon dioxide (CO2) and, according to Fortera, generates 70% fewer emissions than ordinary Portland cement production. The product has undergone third-party testing and meets ASTM standards for use in concrete.",
      "The plant is planned to produce 300,000 tons of cement annually. Fortera already operates a facility in Redding, California, with annual capacity of 15,000 tons.",
      "The agreement provides a long-term demand signal for lower-emission construction materials, potentially giving Fortera greater revenue certainty as it seeks funding for new facilities."
    ],
    "notes": [
      "All claims trace to the Carbon Herald article: multi-year Meta EAC agreement for ~200,000 tons of low-carbon cement; option for Meta to use cement and expand volume/duration; support for planned Ste. Genevieve, Missouri plant; ReAct Cement using captured CO2 with company-reported 70% fewer emissions than OPC; third-party testing and ASTM standards; planned 300,000 t/yr capacity.",
      "Capacity status is correctly framed: Ste. Genevieve is described as 'planned' (300,000 tons annually), and the Redding facility is described as already operating (15,000 tons), consistent with the source.",
      "The candidate is marked secondary and the source is Carbon Herald, a named trade publication reporting the development, so the authority check passes.",
      "Uncertainty field appropriately flags missing signing date, duration, price, EAC methodology, CO2 source, chemistry, energy use, FID, timeline, capex, LCA boundary, and independent verification — none of which appear in the source.",
      "No legal/regulatory claims are made, so legal_status_effective_date is inapplicable and passes.",
      "Only English is provided; no Chinese translation to compare, so translation_meaning passes as inapplicable."
    ],
